<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Sometimes ’mid scenes of deepest gloom,</l><l>Sometimes where Eden’s bowers bloom,</l><l>By waters still, o’er troubled sea,</l><l>Still ’tis His hand that leadeth me.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Lord, I would clasp Thy hand in mine,</l><l>Nor ever murmur or repine;</l><l>Content, whatever lot I see,</l><l>Since it is Thou that leadest me.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>And when my task on earth is done,</l><l>When, by Thy grace, the vict’ry’s won,</l><l>E’en death’s cold wave I will not flee,</l><l>Since Thou in triumph leadest me.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
